From fac4d6f9412c4cffc0bb60bccbb53a317c18a55a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitry B <dimitryB@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:20:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(evm): add Hemi default stablecoins

Enable dollar-string pricing on Hemi mainnet (chain ID 43111) and Hemi
Testnet (chain ID 743111) in the TypeScript SDK.

Hemi mainnet: USDC.e (Stargate bridged, Circle FiatToken v2.2) at
0xad11a8BEb98bbf61dbb1aa0F6d6F2ECD87b35afA, 6 decimals. The token
implements EIP-3009, so no transfer-method override is needed. Its
EIP-712 domain is name "Bridged USDC (Stargate)", version "2"; the
domain separator recomputed from these values matches
DOMAIN_SEPARATOR() on chain.

Hemi Testnet: USDC.e at 0xD47971C7F5B1067d25cd45d30b2c9eb60de96443,
6 decimals. It is a plain ERC-20 with neither EIP-3009 nor EIP-2612, so
the entry uses assetTransferMethod "permit2" and omits supportsEip2612,
like Igra. The token has no version(); the name/version fields are not
sent in extra for this entry and follow the Igra entry's convention.

Also register v1 network names hemi and hemi-testnet, add the two
networks to the default-asset docs table, and cover both entries with
parsePrice and v1-name resolution tests. viem already ships hemi and
hemiSepolia, so the paywall's chain lookup needs no change. Decimals
stay 6, so the generated paywall decimals map is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
